/-!
# Cell structures on the objects of a compactly generated category

Let `D` be a pre-triangulated category with direct sums, and let `E : ι → D` be a family of compact
objects (`CategoryTheory.IsCompactObject`, see
`StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Triangulated.CompactObjects.ThickSubcategory`).

* If a family `E : ι → D` of compact objects generates `D` — the only object receiving only zero
  maps from the shifts `(E i)⟦m⟧` is the zero object — then every object `X` of `D` carries a *cell
  structure*: there is a system `X₀ → X₁ → X₂ → ⋯` with `X = hocolim Xₙ`, whose first term is a
  direct sum of shifts of the `E i`, and each of whose transition morphisms sits in a distinguished
  triangle `Yₙ ⟶ Xₙ ⟶ Xₙ₊₁ ⟶ Yₙ⟦1⟧` with `Yₙ` again a direct sum of shifts of the `E i`. The
  compact generators build every object of `D` by countably many steps of attaching sums of shifted
  cells, exactly as a CW complex is built from spheres.

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.exists_isHomotopyColimit_of_compactlyGenerated`: every object of
  a pre-triangulated category with direct sums generated by a family of compact objects is a
  derived colimit of a system of cell attachments.
* `CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.isHomotopyColimit_of_forall_fac_of_forall_eventually_eq_zero`:
  the gluing half of the previous result, separated off so that it applies to a cell tower built
  by other means — a tower whose terms are compact, say, which the one constructed above is not.

## Implementation notes

*Direct sums of shifts.* "Direct sum of shifts of the `E i`" is the object property
`⨆ J : Type v, ((ObjectProperty.ofObj E).shiftClosure ℤ).colimitsOfShape (Discrete J)`: an object
satisfying it is isomorphic to a coproduct, indexed by some `J : Type v`, of objects each
isomorphic to a shift `(E i)⟦m⟧`. Equivalently, it is an object isomorphic to
`∐ fun j : J ↦ (E (f j))⟦m j⟧` for some `f : J → ι` and `m : J → ℤ`; the lattice-theoretic form is
preferred because it is closed under isomorphisms by construction, is monotone in the family, and
inherits the `ObjectProperty` API.
"Generated by `⨁ E i`" is Definition [Stacks, Tag 09SJ](3) read for a family: no nonzero object is
right orthogonal to all shifts of all the `E i`, i.e.
`((ObjectProperty.ofObj E).shiftClosure ℤ).rightOrthogonal Y → IsZero Y`. This is the spelling used
for the same hypothesis in the Brown representability results, [Stacks, Tags 0A8F and 0A8G], and it
is what [Stacks, Tag 09SL] concludes.

*The cell tower.* The system `(Xₙ, Xₙ → Xₙ₊₁)` is a functor `F : ℕ ⥤ D`, as in the derived colimit
of [Stacks, Tag 090Z] (`Pretriangulated.IsHomotopyColimit`), and the transition morphism is
`F.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n))`. The source's indices start at `1` and Lean's at `0`, so the
source's `X₁` is `F.obj 0`. The tower is the source's: `X₀` is the direct sum of `(E i)⟦m⟧` over
*all* triples `(i, m, φ)` with `φ : (E i)⟦m⟧ ⟶ X`, so that every map from a shift of a generator to
`X` factors through `X₀ ⟶ X`; and given `Xₙ ⟶ X`, the object `Yₙ` is the direct sum over those
triples for which the composition `(E i)⟦m⟧ ⟶ Xₙ ⟶ X` vanishes, `Xₙ₊₁` being the cone of `Yₙ ⟶ Xₙ`.
The map `Xₙ ⟶ X` kills `Yₙ ⟶ Xₙ`, so it extends along `Xₙ ⟶ Xₙ₊₁`, and the resulting map `b` from a
derived colimit `K` of the tower to `X` is an isomorphism: maps to `X` from shifts of the
generators factor through `b`, and maps from shifts of generators to `K` that `b` kills vanish,
because such a map factors through some `Xₙ` (compactness) by a map annihilated by `Xₙ ⟶ X`, hence
through `Yₙ`, hence dies in `Xₙ₊₁`. The cone of `b` therefore receives no nonzero map from a shift
of a generator, so it is zero. The step which carries this is
`eq_zero_of_comp_eq_zero_of_isCompactObject`; it rests on the two halves of "maps out of a compact
object commute with derived colimits" ([Stacks, Tag 094A]), proved here for a system indexed by `ℕ`
because neither is in Mathlib: `exists_eq_comp_of_isCompactObject` (a map from a compact object to
a derived colimit factors through `∐ Xₙ`, because the map `1 - fₙ` of the defining triangle is
injective on maps out of a compact object, `eq_zero_of_comp_telescope_eq_zero`) and
`exists_factor_comp` (such a factorisation goes, after composing with any map out of the direct sum
which is compatible with the transitions, through a single `Xₙ`). That `1 - fₙ` is injective on
maps out of a compact object is an instance of an algebraic fact about direct sums indexed by `ℕ`:
a degree-raising endomorphism has no nonzero fixed point (`eq_zero_of_eq_shiftUp`), since the
degree `n` component of a fixed point is the image of its degree `n - 1` component and vanishes for
`n = 0`. Compactness tests families indexed by the universe in which it is read, so the direct sum
of the groups `A ⟶ Xₙ` over `ℕ` is taken over a lift of `ℕ` to that universe; reindexing a colimit
cofan on `(Xₙ)` along it exhibits the same direct sum (`bijective_cofanMap_ulift`). Both halves are
proved for an arbitrary colimit cofan and for a bare family with explicit transition morphisms —
`eq_zero_of_comp_eq_zero_of_isColimitCofan` and `exists_factor_comp_of_isColimitCofan` — the two
forms above being their specialisations to the chosen coproduct of a functor. The specialisations
inherit the independence of the two universes: the direct sums over `Type w` whose existence is
assumed, and the universe `w` in which compactness is read, are not tied to the hom universe `v`.

*Universes.* In the cell construction the index type `ι` of a generating family lies in the same
universe `v` as the morphisms and as the index types of the assumed direct sums, so that the direct
sum over the triples `(i, m, φ)` is again one of the assumed direct sums, and so that compactness
is tested against exactly the families whose direct sums are assumed to exist. The *gluing* half is
stated without that coincidence: it tests compactness against families indexed by an unrelated
universe `w`, and assumes the direct sums over `Type w`. A derived colimit of a system indexed by
`ℕ` only ever involves `ℕ`-indexed direct sums, so there is nothing to tie the two universes
together, and they do differ in the application that motivates the separation — the derived
category of a differential graded algebra over `R : Type u`, whose morphisms live in `Type (u + 1)`
while its direct sums and its compact objects are indexed by `Type u`. Only `Pretriangulated D` is
assumed for the first two results, which is the source's parenthetical "(pre-)" read as the weaker
hypothesis: the cell construction uses the existence of cones (TR1), the lifting of morphisms (TR3)
and the long exact sequences of a distinguished triangle, and never the octahedron axiom. The full
`IsTriangulated D` is assumed for the last two, as in the source, since the triangulated envelope
is closed under extensions only there.

*Dying at the next stage versus dying eventually.* The cell tower constructed here kills, at each
stage, every cell of that stage which dies in `X`, so a cell annihilated by `Xₙ ⟶ X` dies already
in `Xₙ₊₁`. The gluing step does not need that: it is enough that the cell die in `X_{n+s}` for some
`s`, since along the map out of `∐ Xₙ` the `n`-th coprojection agrees with any later one
precomposed with a transition (`ι_comp_eq_of_distTriang_le`). The weaker hypothesis is what a tower
with compact terms can offer, because such a tower attaches only finitely many cells at a time and
reaches a given cell only at some later stage; so `eq_zero_of_comp_eq_zero_of_isCompactObject` and
the gluing result are stated with it. Closure of compactness under *finite* direct sums
(`isCompactObject_sigma`) is what makes those finite stages compact; it is read off the fact that
the compact objects form a strictly full triangulated subcategory, which is closed under finite
coproducts.

## References

* [Stacks project, Tag 09SN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09SN)
* [Stacks project, Tag 094A](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/094A)
-/

@[expose] public section

universe w v u

/-! ### Cell structures on the objects of a compactly generated category -/

namespace CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated

open Limits ObjectProperty

section CompactlyGenerated

variable (D : Type u) [Category.{v} D] [Preadditive D] [HasShift D ℤ]

/-- A category `D` with a shift by `ℤ` is *compactly generated* if there is a family `E : ι → D`
of compact objects, indexed by a type `ι : Type w`, which is a weak generator: the only objects of
`D` receiving only zero maps from the shifts `(E i)⟦n⟧` are the zero objects. When `D` has direct
sums indexed by `Type w` this says that `⨁ E i` generates `D`, as in Definition
[Stacks, Tag 09SQ] — see `ObjectProperty.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_ofObj_iff`. -/
@[stacks 09SQ]
public def IsCompactlyGenerated : Prop :=
  ∃ (ι : Type w) (E : ι → D),
    (∀ i, IsCompactObject.{w} (E i)) ∧ (ofObj E).IsWeakTriangulatedGenerator

end CompactlyGenerated

section DirectSum

variable {M : ℕ → Type*} [∀ n : ℕ, AddCommGroup (M n)]

/-- The degree-raising endomorphism of the direct sum `⨁ₙ Mₙ` attached to a family of maps
`Tₙ : Mₙ →+ Mₙ₊₁`. The index type is `ℕ` lifted to an arbitrary universe, that of the direct sums
against which compactness is tested. -/
def shiftUp (T : ∀ n : ℕ, M n →+ M (n + 1)) :
    (DirectSum (ULift.{v} ℕ) fun k ↦ M k.down) →+ DirectSum (ULift.{v} ℕ) fun k ↦ M k.down :=
  DirectSum.toAddMonoid fun k ↦
    (DirectSum.of (fun k' : ULift.{v} ℕ ↦ M k'.down) (ULift.up (k.down + 1))).comp (T k.down)

/-- On the `k`-th summand, `shiftUp T` is `T k` landing in the summand of degree `k + 1`. -/
lemma shiftUp_of (T : ∀ n : ℕ, M n →+ M (n + 1)) (k : ULift.{v} ℕ) (g : M k.down) :
    shiftUp T (DirectSum.of (fun k' : ULift.{v} ℕ ↦ M k'.down) k g)
      = DirectSum.of (fun k' : ULift.{v} ℕ ↦ M k'.down) (ULift.up (k.down + 1)) (T k.down g) :=
  DirectSum.toAddMonoid_of _ _ _

/-- The degree `0` component of `shiftUp T x` vanishes: nothing is raised into degree `0`. -/
lemma shiftUp_apply_zero (T : ∀ n : ℕ, M n →+ M (n + 1))
    (x : DirectSum (ULift.{v} ℕ) fun k ↦ M k.down) : shiftUp T x (ULift.up 0) = 0 := by
  induction x using DirectSum.induction_on with
  | zero => simp
  | of k g => rw [shiftUp_of]; exact DirectSum.of_eq_of_ne _ _ _ (by simp)
  | add x y hx hy => simp [hx, hy]

/-- The degree `n + 1` component of `shiftUp T x` is `T n` of the degree `n` component of `x`. -/
lemma shiftUp_apply_succ (T : ∀ n : ℕ, M n →+ M (n + 1))
    (x : DirectSum (ULift.{v} ℕ) fun k ↦ M k.down) (n : ℕ) :
    shiftUp T x (ULift.up (n + 1)) = T n (x (ULift.up n)) := by
  induction x using DirectSum.induction_on with
  | zero => simp
  | of k g =>
    obtain ⟨m⟩ := k
    rw [shiftUp_of]
    by_cases h : m = n
    · subst h
      rw [DirectSum.of_eq_same, DirectSum.of_eq_same]
    · have hne : (ULift.up n : ULift.{v} ℕ) ≠ ULift.up m := by simpa using Ne.symm h
      have hne' : (ULift.up (n + 1) : ULift.{v} ℕ) ≠ ULift.up (m + 1) := by simpa using Ne.symm h
      rw [DirectSum.of_eq_of_ne _ _ _ hne', DirectSum.of_eq_of_ne _ _ _ hne, map_zero]
  | add x y hx hy => simp [hx, hy]

/-- A degree-raising endomorphism of a direct sum indexed by `ℕ` has no nonzero fixed point: the
degree `n` component of a fixed point is the image of its degree `n - 1` component, and its
degree `0` component vanishes. Equivalently, `1 - shiftUp T` is injective. -/
lemma eq_zero_of_eq_shiftUp (T : ∀ n : ℕ, M n →+ M (n + 1))
    {x : DirectSum (ULift.{v} ℕ) fun k ↦ M k.down} (hx : x = shiftUp T x) : x = 0 := by
  have hxn : ∀ n : ℕ, x (ULift.up n) = 0 := by
    intro n
    induction n with
    | zero => rw [hx]; exact shiftUp_apply_zero T x
    | succ n ih => rw [hx, shiftUp_apply_succ, ih, map_zero]
  refine DFinsupp.ext fun k ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨n⟩ := k
  simpa using hxn n

end DirectSum

section Shift

variable {D : Type u} [Category.{v} D] [Preadditive D] [HasShift D ℤ]
  [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor D n).Additive]

/-- If `b : W ⟶ Z` detects the maps to `W` out of `A⟦-1⟧`, it detects, after shifting, the maps
to `W⟦1⟧` out of `A`. -/
lemma eq_zero_of_comp_shift_map_eq_zero {W Z A : D} {b : W ⟶ Z}
    (h : ∀ g : A⟦(-1 : ℤ)⟧ ⟶ W, g ≫ b = 0 → g = 0)
    (ζ : A ⟶ W⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧) (hζ : ζ ≫ b⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧' = 0) : ζ = 0 := by
  have e : A⟦(-1 : ℤ)⟧⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧ ≅ A :=
    (shiftFunctorCompIsoId D (-1 : ℤ) (1 : ℤ) (by simp)).app A
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ : ∃ g : A⟦(-1 : ℤ)⟧ ⟶ W, g⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧' = e.hom ≫ ζ :=
    ⟨(shiftFunctor D (1 : ℤ)).preimage _, (shiftFunctor D (1 : ℤ)).map_preimage _⟩
  have hgb : g ≫ b = 0 := by
    refine (Functor.map_eq_zero_iff (shiftFunctor D (1 : ℤ))).1 ?_
    rw [Functor.map_comp, hg, Category.assoc, hζ, comp_zero]
  rw [← cancel_epi e.hom, comp_zero, ← hg, h g hgb, Functor.map_zero]

end Shift

section Generators

variable {D : Type u} [Category.{v} D] [Preadditive D] [HasZeroObject D] [HasShift D ℤ]
  [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor D n).Additive] [Pretriangulated D]

/-- In a distinguished triangle `W ⟶ Z ⟶ V ⟶ W⟦1⟧` whose first morphism `b` detects the maps to `W`
out of `A⟦-1⟧`, the third morphism kills every map `A ⟶ V`. -/
private lemma comp_eq_zero_of_distTriang_of_forall {W Z V A : D} {b : W ⟶ Z} {g : Z ⟶ V}
    {k : V ⟶ W⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧} (hT : Triangle.mk b g k ∈ distTriang D)
    (h : ∀ g : A⟦(-1 : ℤ)⟧ ⟶ W, g ≫ b = 0 → g = 0) (ζ : A ⟶ V) : ζ ≫ k = 0 :=
  eq_zero_of_comp_shift_map_eq_zero h _
    (by rw [Category.assoc, show k ≫ b⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧' = 0 from comp_distTriang_mor_zero₃₁ _ hT,
      comp_zero])

/-- A morphism `b : K ⟶ X` of a pre-triangulated category is an isomorphism as soon as, for a
shift-stable property of objects `Q` whose right orthogonal consists of zero objects, every map
to `X` from an object satisfying `Q` factors through `b` and every map to `K` from an object
satisfying `Q` that `b` annihilates vanishes. -/
lemma isIso_of_rightOrthogonal_eq_zero {Q : ObjectProperty D} [Q.IsStableUnderShift ℤ]
    (hQ : ∀ Y : D, Q.rightOrthogonal Y → IsZero Y) {K X : D} (b : K ⟶ X)
    (h₁ : ∀ ⦃A : D⦄, Q A → ∀ η : A ⟶ X, ∃ μ : A ⟶ K, η = μ ≫ b)
    (h₂ : ∀ ⦃A : D⦄, Q A → ∀ ζ : A ⟶ K, ζ ≫ b = 0 → ζ = 0) : IsIso b := by
  obtain ⟨Z, g, k, hT⟩ := distinguished_cocone_triangle b
  refine (Triangle.isZero₃_iff_isIso₁ _ hT).1 (hQ _ (fun {A} ξ hA ↦ ?_))
  have hξk : ξ ≫ k = 0 :=
    comp_eq_zero_of_distTriang_of_forall hT (fun g' hg' ↦ h₂ (Q.le_shift (-1 : ℤ) _ hA) g' hg') ξ
  obtain ⟨η, hη⟩ := Triangle.coyoneda_exact₃ _ hT ξ hξk
  obtain ⟨μ, hμ⟩ := h₁ hA η
  rw [hη, hμ, Category.assoc]
  simpa using congrArg (fun t ↦ μ ≫ t) (comp_distTriang_mor_zero₁₂ _ hT)

omit [Preadditive D] [HasZeroObject D] [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor D n).Additive]
  [Pretriangulated D] in
/-- An object in the shift-closure of a family `E` is isomorphic to a shift of a member of `E`. -/
private lemma exists_iso_shift_of_prop_shiftClosure {ι : Type*} (E : ι → D) {B : D}
    (hB : ((ofObj E).shiftClosure ℤ) B) : ∃ (i : ι) (m : ℤ), Nonempty (B ≅ (E i)⟦m⟧) := by
  obtain ⟨Y, m, e, hY⟩ := hB
  obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ := (ObjectProperty.ofObj_iff _ _).1 hY
  exact ⟨i, m, ⟨e⟩⟩

/-- A morphism `b : K ⟶ X` is an isomorphism as soon as every map to `X` from a shift of a member
of a family `E` whose right orthogonal consists of zero objects factors through `b`, and every
such map to `K` that `b` annihilates vanishes: the criterion
`isIso_of_rightOrthogonal_eq_zero` for the shift-closure of `E`, tested on the shifts `(E i)⟦m⟧`
themselves. -/
private lemma isIso_of_ofObj_rightOrthogonal_eq_zero {ι : Type*} (E : ι → D)
    (hE : ∀ Y : D, ((ofObj E).shiftClosure ℤ).rightOrthogonal Y → IsZero Y) {K X : D} (b : K ⟶ X)
    (h₁ : ∀ (i : ι) (m : ℤ) (η : (E i)⟦m⟧ ⟶ X), ∃ μ : (E i)⟦m⟧ ⟶ K, η = μ ≫ b)
    (h₂ : ∀ (i : ι) (m : ℤ) (ζ : (E i)⟦m⟧ ⟶ K), ζ ≫ b = 0 → ζ = 0) : IsIso b := by
  refine isIso_of_rightOrthogonal_eq_zero hE b (fun {B} hB η ↦ ?_) (fun {B} hB ζ hζ ↦ ?_)
  · obtain ⟨i, m, ⟨e⟩⟩ := exists_iso_shift_of_prop_shiftClosure E hB
    obtain ⟨μ, hμ⟩ := h₁ i m (e.inv ≫ η)
    exact ⟨e.hom ≫ μ, by rw [Category.assoc, ← hμ, e.hom_inv_id_assoc]⟩
  · obtain ⟨i, m, ⟨e⟩⟩ := exists_iso_shift_of_prop_shiftClosure E hB
    have h := h₂ i m (e.inv ≫ ζ) (by rw [Category.assoc, hζ, comp_zero])
    simpa using congrArg (fun t ↦ e.hom ≫ t) h

end Generators

/-! ### Morphisms out of a compact object into a direct sum presented by a cofan

A system `(Gₙ, tₙ)` over `ℕ` whose direct sum is presented by a colimit cofan `(V, σₙ)` carries
the endomorphism `a = 1 - t` of `V` determined by `σₙ ≫ a = σₙ - tₙ ≫ σₙ₊₁`. That endomorphism is
injective on the morphisms out of a compact object, and a morphism out of a compact object into
`V` factors through one term of the system after composition with any map compatible with the
transitions. These are the two halves of [Stacks, Tag 094A].

They are stated for an arbitrary colimit cofan rather than for the chosen coproduct `∐ₙ Gₙ`, for
a bare family with explicit transitions rather than for a functor `ℕ ⥤ D`, without a
`HasCoproducts` hypothesis, and with the universe in which compactness is tested independent of
the hom universe: a consumer may hold a `V` and legs `σₙ` that the chosen coproduct matches only
up to unfolding. The forms for the chosen coproduct of a functor `F : ℕ ⥤ D`, which is how the
cell-filtration arguments of this file use them, are the specialisations
`eq_zero_of_comp_telescope_eq_zero` and `exists_factor_comp` of the next section. -/

section Cofan

variable {D : Type u} [Category.{v} D] [Preadditive D]

/-- Compactness of `K`, read against a colimit cofan whose index type `ℕ` has been lifted to the
universe in which compactness is tested. -/
private lemma bijective_cofanMap_ulift (K : D) [hK : IsCompactObject.{w} K] (G : ℕ → D) {V : D}
    (σ : ∀ n, G n ⟶ V) (hσ : IsColimit (Cofan.mk V σ)) :
    Function.Bijective (cofanMap K fun k : ULift.{w} ℕ ↦ σ k.down) :=
  bijective_cofanMap K hK _ (Cofan.isColimitEquivOfEquiv Equiv.ulift _ hσ)

/-- The map `1 - tₙ` of the triangle defining a derived colimit is injective on the morphisms out
of a compact object: half of [Stacks, Tag 094A]. Under the compactness bijection it is
`1 - shiftUp T` for the degree-raising endomorphism given by the transition morphisms, which has
no nonzero fixed point. -/
lemma eq_zero_of_comp_eq_zero_of_isColimitCofan (G : ℕ → D)
    (t : ∀ n, G n ⟶ G (n + 1)) {V : D} (σ : ∀ n, G n ⟶ V) (hσ : IsColimit (Cofan.mk V σ))
    {a : V ⟶ V} (ha : ∀ n, σ n ≫ a = σ n - t n ≫ σ (n + 1))
    (K : D) [IsCompactObject.{w} K] (ψ : K ⟶ V) (hψ : ψ ≫ a = 0) : ψ = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := (bijective_cofanMap_ulift K G σ hσ).2 ψ
  obtain ⟨T, hTof⟩ : ∃ T : ∀ n : ℕ, (K ⟶ G n) →+ (K ⟶ G (n + 1)),
      ∀ (k : ULift.{w} ℕ) (g : K ⟶ G k.down),
        shiftUp T (DirectSum.of (fun k' : ULift.{w} ℕ ↦ (K ⟶ G k'.down)) k g)
          = DirectSum.of (fun k' : ULift.{w} ℕ ↦ (K ⟶ G k'.down)) (ULift.up (k.down + 1))
              (g ≫ t k.down) := by
    refine ⟨fun n ↦ Preadditive.rightComp K (t n), fun k g ↦ ?_⟩
    exact shiftUp_of (M := fun n ↦ (K ⟶ G n)) _ k g
  have hkey : (Preadditive.rightComp K a).comp (cofanMap K fun k : ULift.{w} ℕ ↦ σ k.down)
      = (cofanMap K fun k : ULift.{w} ℕ ↦ σ k.down).comp
        (AddMonoidHom.id _ - shiftUp T) := by
    refine DirectSum.addHom_ext (fun k g ↦ ?_)
    rw [AddMonoidHom.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply, cofanMap_of, AddMonoidHom.coe_comp,
      Function.comp_apply, AddMonoidHom.sub_apply, AddMonoidHom.id_apply, hTof, map_sub,
      cofanMap_of, cofanMap_of]
    show (g ≫ σ k.down) ≫ a = _
    rw [Category.assoc, ha, Preadditive.comp_sub, Category.assoc]
  have hxS : x = shiftUp T x := by
    have h : (cofanMap K fun k : ULift.{w} ℕ ↦ σ k.down) (x - shiftUp T x)
        = (cofanMap K fun k : ULift.{w} ℕ ↦ σ k.down) 0 := by
      rw [map_zero, ← hψ, ← hx]
      exact (DFunLike.congr_fun hkey x).symm
    rw [← sub_eq_zero]
    exact (bijective_cofanMap_ulift K G σ hσ).1 h
  rw [← hx, eq_zero_of_eq_shiftUp T hxS, map_zero]

omit [Preadditive D] in
/-- Along a map out of a direct-sum presentation which is compatible with the transition
morphisms, the `n`-th leg agrees with any later leg up to precomposition with transitions. -/
private lemma exists_factor_eq (G : ℕ → D) (t : ∀ n, G n ⟶ G (n + 1)) {V : D}
    (σ : ∀ n, G n ⟶ V) {W : D} (r : V ⟶ W)
    (hr : ∀ n : ℕ, σ n ≫ r = t n ≫ σ (n + 1) ≫ r) {n N : ℕ} (h : n ≤ N) :
    ∃ c : G n ⟶ G N, σ n ≫ r = c ≫ σ N ≫ r := by
  induction N, h using Nat.le_induction with
  | base => exact ⟨𝟙 _, by simp⟩
  | succ N hN ih =>
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := ih
    exact ⟨c ≫ t N, by rw [hc, hr N]; simp⟩

/-- Along a map out of a direct sum of the terms of a system which is compatible with the
transition morphisms, a morphism from a compact object factors through a single term: the other
half of [Stacks, Tag 094A]. -/
lemma exists_factor_comp_of_isColimitCofan (G : ℕ → D) (t : ∀ n, G n ⟶ G (n + 1)) {V : D}
    (σ : ∀ n, G n ⟶ V) (hσ : IsColimit (Cofan.mk V σ)) {W : D} (r : V ⟶ W)
    (hr : ∀ n : ℕ, σ n ≫ r = t n ≫ σ (n + 1) ≫ r)
    (K : D) [IsCompactObject.{w} K] (ψ : K ⟶ V) :
    ∃ (N : ℕ) (ρ : K ⟶ G N), ψ ≫ r = ρ ≫ σ N ≫ r := by
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := (bijective_cofanMap_ulift K G σ hσ).2 ψ
  induction x using DirectSum.induction_on with
  | zero => exact ⟨0, 0, by simp⟩
  | of k g => exact ⟨k.down, g, by rw [cofanMap_of, Category.assoc]⟩
  | add x y hx hy =>
    obtain ⟨N₁, ρ₁, h₁⟩ := hx
    obtain ⟨N₂, ρ₂, h₂⟩ := hy
    obtain ⟨c₁, hc₁⟩ := exists_factor_eq G t σ r hr (le_max_left N₁ N₂)
    obtain ⟨c₂, hc₂⟩ := exists_factor_eq G t σ r hr (le_max_right N₁ N₂)
    refine ⟨max N₁ N₂, ρ₁ ≫ c₁ + ρ₂ ≫ c₂, ?_⟩
    rw [map_add, Preadditive.add_comp, h₁, h₂, hc₁, hc₂, Preadditive.add_comp]
    simp

end Cofan

section Compact

variable {D : Type u} [Category.{v} D] [Preadditive D] [HasCoproducts.{w} D]

/-- The map `1 - fₙ` out of `∐ F.obj` whose cone is the derived colimit of the system `F`. -/
private noncomputable def telescope (F : ℕ ⥤ D) : ∐ F.obj ⟶ ∐ F.obj :=
  Limits.Sigma.desc fun n ↦
    Limits.Sigma.ι F.obj n - F.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n)) ≫ Limits.Sigma.ι F.obj (n + 1)

private lemma ι_comp_telescope (F : ℕ ⥤ D) (n : ℕ) :
    Limits.Sigma.ι F.obj n ≫ telescope F
      = Limits.Sigma.ι F.obj n - F.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n)) ≫ Limits.Sigma.ι F.obj (n + 1) :=
  Limits.Sigma.ι_desc _ _

/-- The telescope map is killed by the map out of `∐ F.obj` induced by a compatible family of
morphisms `a n : F.obj n ⟶ X`. -/
private lemma telescope_comp_desc (F : ℕ ⥤ D) {X : D} (a : ∀ n : ℕ, F.obj n ⟶ X)
    (ha : ∀ n : ℕ, F.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n)) ≫ a (n + 1) = a n) :
    telescope F ≫ Limits.Sigma.desc a = 0 := by
  refine Limits.Sigma.hom_ext _ _ (fun n ↦ ?_)
  rw [← Category.assoc, ι_comp_telescope, Preadditive.sub_comp]
  simp [ha n]

/-- The map `1 - fₙ` of the triangle defining a derived colimit is injective on the maps out of a
compact object: half of [Stacks, Tag 094A]. It is
`eq_zero_of_comp_eq_zero_of_isColimitCofan` for the system of a functor `F : ℕ ⥤ D` presented by
its chosen coproduct, whose legs exhibit `∐ F.obj` as a colimit cofan by
`coproductIsCoproduct`. The universe `w` in which compactness is read is independent of the hom
universe: the cofan form it specialises is already stated that way, and the consumer
`DifferentialGradedModule.exists_isHomotopyColimit_isCompactObject_of_countable_cohomology` needs
the two to differ. -/
private lemma eq_zero_of_comp_telescope_eq_zero (F : ℕ ⥤ D) (A : D) [IsCompactObject.{w} A]
    (ψ : A ⟶ ∐ F.obj) (hψ : ψ ≫ telescope F = 0) : ψ = 0 :=
  eq_zero_of_comp_eq_zero_of_isColimitCofan F.obj
    (fun n ↦ F.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n))) (Limits.Sigma.ι F.obj)
    (coproductIsCoproduct F.obj) (ι_comp_telescope F) A ψ hψ

/-- Along a map out of the direct sum of the terms of a system which is compatible with the
transition morphisms, a map from a compact object factors through a single term: the other half
of [Stacks, Tag 094A]. It is `exists_factor_comp_of_isColimitCofan` for the system of a functor
`F : ℕ ⥤ D` presented by its chosen coproduct. -/
private lemma exists_factor_comp (F : ℕ ⥤ D) {W : D} (r : ∐ F.obj ⟶ W)
    (hr : ∀ n : ℕ, Limits.Sigma.ι F.obj n ≫ r
      = F.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n)) ≫ Limits.Sigma.ι F.obj (n + 1) ≫ r)
    (A : D) [IsCompactObject.{w} A] (ψ : A ⟶ ∐ F.obj) :
    ∃ (N : ℕ) (ρ : A ⟶ F.obj N), ψ ≫ r = ρ ≫ Limits.Sigma.ι F.obj N ≫ r :=
  exists_factor_comp_of_isColimitCofan F.obj (fun n ↦ F.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n)))
    (Limits.Sigma.ι F.obj) (coproductIsCoproduct F.obj) r hr A ψ

end Compact

section Tower

variable {D : Type u} [Category.{v} D] [Preadditive D] [HasZeroObject D] [HasShift D ℤ]
  [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor D n).Additive] [Pretriangulated D] [HasCoproducts.{v} D]
  {ι : Type v}

/-- The cells of an object `Z` relative to a family `E`: triples `(i, m, φ)` with
`φ : (E i)⟦m⟧ ⟶ Z`. -/
private abbrev CellIndex (E : ι → D) (Z : D) : Type v := Σ (i : ι) (m : ℤ), ((E i)⟦m⟧ ⟶ Z)

/-- The shifted generator carried by a cell. -/
private abbrev cellObj (E : ι → D) {Z : D} (t : CellIndex E Z) : D := (E t.1)⟦t.2.1⟧

/-- The cells of `Z` that die in `X`: those triples `(i, m, φ)` for which the composition of `φ`
with `a : Z ⟶ X` vanishes. -/
private abbrev DeadCellIndex (E : ι → D) {Z X : D} (a : Z ⟶ X) : Type v :=
  {t : CellIndex E Z // t.2.2 ≫ a = 0}

/-- The shifted generator carried by a cell that dies in `X`. -/
private abbrev deadCellObj (E : ι → D) {Z X : D} (a : Z ⟶ X) (t : DeadCellIndex E a) : D :=
  cellObj E t.1

/-- The attaching map of the cells of `Z` that die in `X`. -/
private noncomputable def deadCellAttach (E : ι → D) {Z X : D} (a : Z ⟶ X) :
    ∐ deadCellObj E a ⟶ Z :=
  Limits.Sigma.desc fun t ↦ t.1.2.2

omit [HasZeroObject D] [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor D n).Additive] [Pretriangulated D] in
private lemma ι_comp_deadCellAttach (E : ι → D) {Z X : D} (a : Z ⟶ X)
    (t : DeadCellIndex E a) :
    Limits.Sigma.ι (deadCellObj E a) t ≫ deadCellAttach E a = t.1.2.2 :=
  Limits.Sigma.ι_desc _ _

omit [HasZeroObject D] [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor D n).Additive] [Pretriangulated D] in
private lemma deadCellAttach_comp (E : ι → D) {Z X : D} (a : Z ⟶ X) :
    deadCellAttach E a ≫ a = 0 := by
  refine Limits.Sigma.hom_ext _ _ (fun t ↦ ?_)
  rw [← Category.assoc, ι_comp_deadCellAttach, comp_zero]
  exact t.2

/-- A stage of the cell tower over `X`: an object of `D` with a morphism to `X`. -/
private structure Stage (X : D) where
  /-- the object of the stage -/
  obj : D
  /-- the structure morphism to `X` -/
  hom : obj ⟶ X

/-- One step of the cell tower: the cone on the cells of a stage that die in `X`, together with
the induced structure morphism to `X` and the distinguished triangle. -/
private structure StepData (E : ι → D) {X : D} (s : Stage X) where
  /-- the next stage -/
  next : Stage X
  /-- the transition morphism -/
  hom : s.obj ⟶ next.obj
  /-- the third morphism of the distinguished triangle -/
  shift : next.obj ⟶ (∐ deadCellObj E s.hom)⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧
  /-- the transition morphism is the cone on the dead cells -/
  triangle : Triangle.mk (deadCellAttach E s.hom) hom shift ∈ distTriang D
  /-- the structure morphisms are compatible with the transition -/
  comm : hom ≫ next.hom = s.hom

private lemma nonempty_stepData (E : ι → D) {X : D} (s : Stage X) : Nonempty (StepData E s) := by
  obtain ⟨Z, g, k, hT⟩ := distinguished_cocone_triangle (deadCellAttach E s.hom)
  obtain ⟨a', ha'⟩ := Triangle.yoneda_exact₂ _ hT s.hom (deadCellAttach_comp E s.hom)
  exact ⟨⟨⟨Z, a'⟩, g, k, hT, ha'.symm⟩⟩

/-- The chosen step out of a stage. -/
private noncomputable def stepData (E : ι → D) {X : D} (s : Stage X) : StepData E s :=
  (nonempty_stepData E s).some

/-- A morphism to a stage from a shift of a generator which the structure morphism to `X`
annihilates dies in the next stage: it is one of the cells attached there. -/
private lemma comp_stepData_hom_eq_zero (E : ι → D) {X : D} (s : Stage X) (i : ι) (m : ℤ)
    (ρ : (E i)⟦m⟧ ⟶ s.obj) (hρ : ρ ≫ s.hom = 0) : ρ ≫ (stepData E s).hom = 0 := by
  have h0 : deadCellAttach E s.hom ≫ (stepData E s).hom = 0 :=
    comp_distTriang_mor_zero₁₂ _ (stepData E s).triangle
  have hfac : Limits.Sigma.ι (deadCellObj E s.hom) (⟨⟨i, m, ρ⟩, hρ⟩ : DeadCellIndex E s.hom) ≫
      deadCellAttach E s.hom = ρ := ι_comp_deadCellAttach E s.hom _
  rw [← hfac, Category.assoc, h0, comp_zero]

/-- The stages of the cell tower over `X` starting at `s₀`. -/
private noncomputable def tower (E : ι → D) {X : D} (s₀ : Stage X) : ℕ → Stage X := fun n ↦
  Nat.rec s₀ (fun _ s ↦ (stepData E s).next) n

/-- The cell tower over `X` starting at `s₀`, as a system of objects indexed by `ℕ`. -/
private noncomputable def cellTower (E : ι → D) {X : D} (s₀ : Stage X) : ℕ ⥤ D :=
  Functor.ofSequence (X := fun n ↦ (tower E s₀ n).obj)
    fun n ↦ (stepData E (tower E s₀ n)).hom

private lemma cellTower_map_succ (E : ι → D) {X : D} (s₀ : Stage X) (n : ℕ) :
    (cellTower E s₀).map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n)) = (stepData E (tower E s₀ n)).hom :=
  Functor.ofSequence_map_homOfLE_succ _ n

/-- The zeroth stage of the cell tower over `X`: the direct sum of all the cells of `X`. -/
private noncomputable def baseStage (E : ι → D) (X : D) : Stage X :=
  ⟨∐ (fun t : CellIndex E X ↦ cellObj E t), Limits.Sigma.desc fun t ↦ t.2.2⟩

private lemma cellTower_obj_zero (E : ι → D) (X : D) :
    (cellTower E (baseStage E X)).obj 0 = ∐ (fun t : CellIndex E X ↦ cellObj E t) := rfl

omit [Preadditive D] [HasZeroObject D] [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor D n).Additive]
  [Pretriangulated D] in
/-- A direct sum of shifts of the `E i` is a colimit, indexed by a type of the universe of the
ambient direct sums, of objects in the shift-closure of the family. -/
private lemma prop_iSup_colimitsOfShape_sigmaObj (E : ι → D) {J : Type v} (Z : J → D)
    (hZ : ∀ j, ((ofObj E).shiftClosure ℤ) (Z j)) :
    (⨆ J : Type v, ((ofObj E).shiftClosure ℤ).colimitsOfShape (Discrete J)) (∐ Z) := by
  rw [ObjectProperty.prop_iSup_iff]
  exact ⟨J, ⟨ObjectProperty.ColimitOfShape.colimit (Discrete.functor Z) (fun j ↦ hZ j.as)⟩⟩

omit [Preadditive D] [HasZeroObject D] [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor D n).Additive]
  [Pretriangulated D] [HasCoproducts.{v} D] in
private lemma prop_shiftClosure_shift (E : ι → D) (i : ι) (m : ℤ) :
    ((ofObj E).shiftClosure ℤ) ((E i)⟦m⟧) :=
  ⟨E i, m, Iso.refl _, (ObjectProperty.ofObj_iff _ _).2 ⟨i, rfl⟩⟩

/-- The cell tower over `X`: a system `F` with compatible morphisms `a n : F.obj n ⟶ X` such that
every map to `X` from a shift of a generator factors through `a 0`, every map from a shift of a
generator to `F.obj n` annihilated by `a n` dies in `F.obj (n + 1)`, the term `F.obj 0` is a
direct sum of shifts of the generators, and each transition morphism is the cone on such a direct
sum. -/
private lemma exists_cellTower (E : ι → D) (X : D) :
    ∃ (F : ℕ ⥤ D) (a : ∀ n : ℕ, F.obj n ⟶ X),
      (∀ n : ℕ, F.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n)) ≫ a (n + 1) = a n) ∧
      (∀ (i : ι) (m : ℤ) (ψ : (E i)⟦m⟧ ⟶ X), ∃ ρ : (E i)⟦m⟧ ⟶ F.obj 0, ψ = ρ ≫ a 0) ∧
      (∀ (n : ℕ) (i : ι) (m : ℤ) (ρ : (E i)⟦m⟧ ⟶ F.obj n), ρ ≫ a n = 0 →
        ρ ≫ F.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n)) = 0) ∧
      (⨆ J : Type v, ((ofObj E).shiftClosure ℤ).colimitsOfShape (Discrete J)) (F.obj 0) ∧
      (∀ n : ℕ, ∃ Y : D,
        (⨆ J : Type v, ((ofObj E).shiftClosure ℤ).colimitsOfShape (Discrete J)) Y ∧
        ∃ (f : Y ⟶ F.obj n) (g : F.obj (n + 1) ⟶ Y⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧),
          Triangle.mk f (F.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n))) g ∈ distTriang D) := by
  refine ⟨cellTower E (baseStage E X), fun n ↦ (tower E (baseStage E X) n).hom, fun n ↦ ?_,
    fun i m ψ ↦ ?_, fun n i m ρ hρ ↦ ?_, ?_, fun n ↦ ?_⟩
  · rw [cellTower_map_succ]
    exact (stepData E (tower E (baseStage E X) n)).comm
  · exact ⟨Limits.Sigma.ι (fun t : CellIndex E X ↦ cellObj E t) ⟨i, m, ψ⟩,
      (Limits.Sigma.ι_desc (fun t : CellIndex E X ↦ (t.2.2 : cellObj E t ⟶ X)) ⟨i, m, ψ⟩).symm⟩
  · rw [cellTower_map_succ]
    exact comp_stepData_hom_eq_zero E _ i m ρ hρ
  · rw [cellTower_obj_zero]
    exact prop_iSup_colimitsOfShape_sigmaObj E _ (fun t ↦ prop_shiftClosure_shift E t.1 t.2.1)
  · refine ⟨∐ deadCellObj E ((tower E (baseStage E X) n).hom), ?_,
      deadCellAttach E ((tower E (baseStage E X) n).hom),
      (stepData E (tower E (baseStage E X) n)).shift, ?_⟩
    · exact prop_iSup_colimitsOfShape_sigmaObj E _
        (fun t ↦ prop_shiftClosure_shift E t.1.1 t.1.2.1)
    · rw [cellTower_map_succ]
      exact (stepData E (tower E (baseStage E X) n)).triangle

end Tower

section HomotopyColimit

variable {D : Type u} [Category.{v} D] [Preadditive D] [HasZeroObject D] [HasShift D ℤ]
  [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor D n).Additive] [Pretriangulated D] [HasCoproducts.{w} D]
  {F : ℕ ⥤ D} {K X : D} {p : ∐ F.obj ⟶ K} {q : K ⟶ (∐ F.obj)⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧}

/-- In the triangle defining a derived colimit `K` of the system `F`, the structure morphism
`p : ∐ F.obj ⟶ K` is compatible with the transition morphisms. -/
private lemma ι_comp_eq_of_distTriang (hT : Triangle.mk (telescope F) p q ∈ distTriang D) (n : ℕ) :
    Limits.Sigma.ι F.obj n ≫ p
      = F.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n)) ≫ Limits.Sigma.ι F.obj (n + 1) ≫ p := by
  have h0 : telescope F ≫ p = 0 := comp_distTriang_mor_zero₁₂ _ hT
  have h : (Limits.Sigma.ι F.obj n ≫ telescope F) ≫ p = 0 := by
    rw [Category.assoc, h0, comp_zero]
  rwa [ι_comp_telescope, Preadditive.sub_comp, sub_eq_zero, Category.assoc] at h

/-- The same, for an arbitrary later index: along the map from a derived colimit, the `n`-th
coprojection agrees with the `n'`-th one precomposed with the transition `F.obj n ⟶ F.obj n'`. -/
private lemma ι_comp_eq_of_distTriang_le (hT : Triangle.mk (telescope F) p q ∈ distTriang D)
    {n n' : ℕ} (h : n ≤ n') :
    Limits.Sigma.ι F.obj n ≫ p = F.map (homOfLE h) ≫ Limits.Sigma.ι F.obj n' ≫ p := by
  induction n', h using Nat.le_induction with
  | base => simp
  | succ N hN ih =>
    rw [ih, ι_comp_eq_of_distTriang hT N, ← Category.assoc, ← F.map_comp, homOfLE_comp]

omit [Preadditive D] [HasZeroObject D] [HasShift D ℤ]
  [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor D n).Additive] [Pretriangulated D] in
/-- The composition of the `n`-th coprojection with the map from a derived colimit induced by a
compatible family `a n : F.obj n ⟶ X` is `a n`. -/
private lemma ι_comp_comp_eq {a : ∀ n : ℕ, F.obj n ⟶ X} {b : K ⟶ X}
    (hb : Limits.Sigma.desc a = p ≫ b) (n : ℕ) : Limits.Sigma.ι F.obj n ≫ p ≫ b = a n := by
  rw [← hb, Limits.Sigma.ι_desc]

/-- A map from a compact object to a derived colimit of `F` factors through `∐ F.obj`: the third
map of the defining triangle annihilates it, because `1 - fₙ` is injective on maps out of a
compact object. Compactness of the shift `A⟦-1⟧` is all that is used. -/
private lemma exists_eq_comp_of_isCompactObject (hT : Triangle.mk (telescope F) p q ∈ distTriang D)
    (A : D) [IsCompactObject.{w} (A⟦(-1 : ℤ)⟧)] (ζ : A ⟶ K) : ∃ ψ : A ⟶ ∐ F.obj, ζ = ψ ≫ p := by
  exact Triangle.coyoneda_exact₃ _ hT _ (comp_eq_zero_of_distTriang_of_forall hT
    (fun g hg ↦ eq_zero_of_comp_telescope_eq_zero F _ g hg) ζ)

/-- The step which carries [Stacks, Tag 09SN]. Let `K` be a derived colimit of a system `F` whose
terms map compatibly to `X` by maps `a n` inducing `b : K ⟶ X`, and assume that a map from `A` to
a term which `a n` annihilates dies in *some* later term. Then a map from `A` to `K` which `b`
annihilates vanishes: it factors through `∐ F.obj`, hence — `A` being compact — through a single
term `F.obj N` by a map which `a N` annihilates, and that map dies in some `F.obj N'`.

Dying at some later stage, rather than at the next one, is what a diagonal enumeration of the
cells to be killed delivers: at the stage where a given cell is reached only finitely many cells
are attached, so a cell present at stage `n` is in general killed well after stage `n + 1`. -/
private lemma eq_zero_of_comp_eq_zero_of_isCompactObject
    (hT : Triangle.mk (telescope F) p q ∈ distTriang D) {a : ∀ n : ℕ, F.obj n ⟶ X} {b : K ⟶ X}
    (hb : Limits.Sigma.desc a = p ≫ b) (A : D) [IsCompactObject.{w} A]
    [IsCompactObject.{w} (A⟦(-1 : ℤ)⟧)]
    (hdead : ∀ (n : ℕ) (ρ : A ⟶ F.obj n), ρ ≫ a n = 0 →
      ∃ s : ℕ, ρ ≫ F.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_add_right n s)) = 0)
    (ζ : A ⟶ K) (hζ : ζ ≫ b = 0) : ζ = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨ψ, rfl⟩ := exists_eq_comp_of_isCompactObject hT A ζ
  obtain ⟨N, ρ, hρ⟩ := exists_factor_comp F p (ι_comp_eq_of_distTriang hT) A ψ
  have hρa : ρ ≫ a N = 0 := by
    rw [← ι_comp_comp_eq hb N, show ρ ≫ Limits.Sigma.ι F.obj N ≫ p ≫ b
      = (ρ ≫ Limits.Sigma.ι F.obj N ≫ p) ≫ b by simp, ← hρ, hζ]
  obtain ⟨s, hdρ⟩ := hdead N ρ hρa
  rw [hρ, ι_comp_eq_of_distTriang_le hT (Nat.le_add_right N s), ← Category.assoc, hdρ, zero_comp]

end HomotopyColimit

section Glue

variable {D : Type u} [Category.{v} D] [Preadditive D] [HasZeroObject D] [HasShift D ℤ]
  [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor D n).Additive] [Pretriangulated D] [HasCoproducts.{w} D]

/-- **A cell tower with compatible maps to `X` exhibits `X` as a derived colimit.** Let `E : ι → D`
be a family of compact objects whose shifts generate `D`, i.e. the only objects right orthogonal
to all of them are the zero objects. Let `F : ℕ ⥤ D` be a system whose terms map compatibly to `X`
by maps `a n`, and suppose

* every map to `X` from a shift of a generator factors through some term `F.obj n`, and
* every map to a term `F.obj n` from a shift of a generator which `a n` annihilates dies in
  *some* later term `F.obj (n + s)`.

Then `X = hocolim F`.

This is the gluing half of [Stacks, Tag 09SN], separated from the construction of the tower so
that it can be applied to a tower built by other means — in particular to one whose terms are
compact, which the tower of
`CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.exists_isHomotopyColimit_of_compactlyGenerated` is not, since that
one attaches all cells at once. The map `b : hocolim F ⟶ X` induced by the `a n` is an
isomorphism by the generation criterion `isIso_of_ofObj_rightOrthogonal_eq_zero`: the first
hypothesis makes it surjective on maps out of a shift of a generator and the second, through
`eq_zero_of_comp_eq_zero_of_isCompactObject`, injective.

Compactness is tested here against families indexed by a universe `w` unrelated to the universe
of the morphisms of `D`, as are the direct sums assumed to exist: a derived colimit of a system
indexed by `ℕ` only ever involves `ℕ`-indexed direct sums, so there is no reason to tie the two,
and the derived category of a differential graded algebra is an example where they differ. -/
public theorem isHomotopyColimit_of_forall_fac_of_forall_eventually_eq_zero
    {ι : Type*} (E : ι → D) [∀ i, IsCompactObject.{w} (E i)]
    (hE : ∀ Y : D, ((ofObj E).shiftClosure ℤ).rightOrthogonal Y → IsZero Y) {X : D} (F : ℕ ⥤ D)
    (a : ∀ n : ℕ, F.obj n ⟶ X)
    (hacomm : ∀ n : ℕ, F.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n)) ≫ a (n + 1) = a n)
    (hbase : ∀ (i : ι) (m : ℤ) (ψ : (E i)⟦m⟧ ⟶ X),
      ∃ (n : ℕ) (ρ : (E i)⟦m⟧ ⟶ F.obj n), ψ = ρ ≫ a n)
    (hdead : ∀ (n : ℕ) (i : ι) (m : ℤ) (ρ : (E i)⟦m⟧ ⟶ F.obj n), ρ ≫ a n = 0 →
      ∃ s : ℕ, ρ ≫ F.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_add_right n s)) = 0) :
    IsHomotopyColimit F X := by
  obtain ⟨K, p, q, hT⟩ := distinguished_cocone_triangle (telescope F)
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ : ∃ b : K ⟶ X, Limits.Sigma.desc a = p ≫ b :=
    Triangle.yoneda_exact₂ _ hT _ (telescope_comp_desc F a hacomm)
  have hiso : IsIso b := by
    refine isIso_of_ofObj_rightOrthogonal_eq_zero E hE b (fun i m η ↦ ?_) (fun i m ζ hζ ↦ ?_)
    · obtain ⟨n, ρ, hρ⟩ := hbase i m η
      exact ⟨ρ ≫ Limits.Sigma.ι F.obj n ≫ p, by rw [hρ, ← ι_comp_comp_eq hb n]; simp⟩
    · have h : IsCompactObject.{w} ((E i)⟦m⟧) := isCompactObject_shift inferInstance m
      have : IsCompactObject.{w} (((E i)⟦m⟧)⟦(-1 : ℤ)⟧) := isCompactObject_shift h (-1)
      exact eq_zero_of_comp_eq_zero_of_isCompactObject hT hb _
        (fun n ρ hρ ↦ hdead n i m ρ hρ) ζ hζ
  refine ⟨p ≫ b, (asIso b).inv ≫ q, ?_⟩
  exact isomorphic_distinguished _ hT _ (Triangle.isoMk _ _ (Iso.refl _) (Iso.refl _)
    (asIso b).symm (by simp [telescope]) (by simp) (by simp))

end Glue

section CellStructure

variable {D : Type u} [Category.{v} D] [Preadditive D] [HasZeroObject D] [HasShift D ℤ]
  [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor D n).Additive] [Pretriangulated D] [HasCoproducts.{v} D]

/-- **Stacks 09SN**. Let `D` be a pre-triangulated category with direct sums and let `E : ι → D`
be a family of compact objects such that `⨁ E i` generates `D`, i.e. the only objects right
orthogonal to all shifts of the `E i` are the zero objects. Then every object `X` of `D` is a
derived colimit `X = hocolim Xₙ` of a system `F : ℕ ⥤ D` whose first term `F.obj 0` is a direct
sum of shifts of the `E i` and each of whose transition morphisms `Xₙ ⟶ Xₙ₊₁` fits into a
distinguished triangle `Yₙ ⟶ Xₙ ⟶ Xₙ₊₁ ⟶ Yₙ⟦1⟧` with `Yₙ` a direct sum of shifts of the `E i`. -/
@[stacks 09SN]
public theorem exists_isHomotopyColimit_of_compactlyGenerated
    {ι : Type v} (E : ι → D) [∀ i, IsCompactObject.{v} (E i)]
    (hE : ∀ Y : D, ((ofObj E).shiftClosure ℤ).rightOrthogonal Y → IsZero Y) (X : D) :
    ∃ F : ℕ ⥤ D,
      IsHomotopyColimit F X ∧
      (⨆ J : Type v, ((ofObj E).shiftClosure ℤ).colimitsOfShape (Discrete J)) (F.obj 0) ∧
      ∀ n : ℕ, ∃ Y : D,
        (⨆ J : Type v, ((ofObj E).shiftClosure ℤ).colimitsOfShape (Discrete J)) Y ∧
        ∃ (f : Y ⟶ F.obj n) (g : F.obj (n + 1) ⟶ Y⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧),
          Triangle.mk f (F.map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ n))) g ∈ distTriang D := by
  obtain ⟨F, a, hacomm, hbase, hdead, hzero, htri⟩ := exists_cellTower E X
  refine ⟨F, isHomotopyColimit_of_forall_fac_of_forall_eventually_eq_zero E hE F a hacomm
    (fun i m ψ ↦ ?_) fun n i m ρ hρ ↦ ⟨1, hdead n i m ρ hρ⟩, hzero, htri⟩
  obtain ⟨ρ, hρ⟩ := hbase i m ψ
  exact ⟨0, ρ, hρ⟩

end CellStructure

end CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated

